latest_plan = "Based on the reflection, here's a step-by-step plan to solve the challenge:\n\n1. Analyze the Initial Grid:\n   - Identify all unique colors present in the grid.\n   - Determine the initial pattern and distribution of each color.\n   - Calculate the frequency of each color.\n\n2. Create a Target Distribution:\n   - Based on the initial frequencies, create a target distribution for each color in the expanded grid.\n   - Ensure that even colors with low initial frequency get a minimum target to ensure visibility.\n\n3. Pattern Recognition and Template Creation:\n   - For each color, analyze its initial arrangement (e.g., line, cluster, isolated, etc.).\n   - Create expansion templates for each color based on its initial pattern.\n\n4. Multi-stage Expansion Process:\n   a. Pattern-based Expansion:\n      - For each color, use its template to expand outwards from its initial positions.\n      - Prioritize maintaining the essence of the original pattern.\n\n   b. Boundary Interaction:\n      - Handle cases where expanding colors meet at boundaries.\n      - Use the target distribution to resolve conflicts, favoring colors that need more representation.\n\n   c. Fill Empty Spaces:\n      - After initial expansion, fill remaining empty spaces.\n      - Use a combination of pattern extension and weighted random filling based on target distributions.\n\n   d. Connectivity Enhancement:\n      - Ensure that same-color regions are connected where possible.\n      - Create paths between isolated instances of the same color.\n\n5. Symmetry and Balance Adjustments:\n   - Implement symmetry checks and adjustments, particularly for the horizontal axis.\n   - Fine-tune the distribution to match target frequencies more closely.\n\n6. Border Maintenance:\n   - Ensure the black border is maintained throughout the process.\n\n7. Iterative Refinement:\n   - Repeat steps 4-6 for a few iterations to achieve better balance and pattern preservation.\n\n8. Final Adjustments:\n   - Make final tweaks to ensure all original color positions are preserved.\n   - Perform a last pass of empty space filling and connectivity enhancement.\n\n9. Validation:\n   - Check that the final grid meets all requirements:\n     - All original color positions are preserved.\n     - The black border is intact.\n     - Each color has been expanded.\n     - The overall pattern essence is maintained.\n\n10. Return the Transformed Grid:\n    - Output the final, expanded grid that meets all the challenge criteria.\n\nThis plan takes into account the nuanced requirements observed in the reflection, balancing pattern preservation with expansion, ensuring color balance, maintaining connectivity, and creating a harmonious overall result. The iterative nature of the process allows for fine-tuning and adjustment to achieve the best possible outcome."
